        "max_iterations": 8,
        "outcome": "success",
        "result": "{\"action\":\"synthesize\",\"reason\":\"Subtopic: MQTT vs NATS \u2014 latency + memory footprint on constrained ARM (Raspberry Pi class) edge devices\\n\\nEvidence gathered: MQTT (Mosquitto) runs under 2MB resident on Raspberry Pi-class hardware; QoS 0 publishes complete in well under a millisecond. NATS server binary ~10MB, runtime ~30MB resident, but offers subject-hierarchy pub/sub PLUS request-reply in one broker; JetStream adds persistence. Forwarding to SYNTHESIZE to compose the comparison \u2014 actors (MQTT brokers, NATS servers, ARM hardware class) and integration points (broker \u2192 edge sensor).\"}"
      },
